  "body": "  Unit 3 Class Creation:     Practice 3.C: Determine the result or output based on code that contains procedural abstractions.    Practice 3.D: Explain why a code segment will not compile or work as intended and modify the code to correct the error.    LO 3.5.A Develop code to define behaviors of an object through methods written in a class using primitive values and determine the result of calling these methods.     Consider the following class definition. The class does not compile.   public class Student { private int id; public void getId() { return id; } }   The accessor method getId is intended to return the id of a Student object. Which of the following best explains why the class does not compile?      The getId method should be declared as private.       The getId method should have a parameter.       The getId method should not return a value.       The getId method should not have a return type.       The getId method should have int as its return type.       I don’t know this yet.      "
