  "number": "2.6.1",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  For what values of x and y will the code below print true? Try out different values of x and y to check your answer.    public class Test1 { public static void main(String[] args) { int x = 2; int y = 3; System.out.println(!(x < 3 && y > 2)); } }  import static org.junit.Assert.*; import org.junit.*; import java.io.*; public class RunestoneTests extends CodeTestHelper { @Test public void testChangedCode() { String origCode = \"public class Test1 {public static void main(String[] args) { int x = 2; int y = 3;\" + \" System.out.println(!(x < 3 && y > 2)); } }\"; boolean changed = codeChanged(origCode); assertTrue(changed); } }   "
