  "body": "  Which of the following expressions return the right value for the day of the week (2) for Jan. 8th 2019 given that firstDayOfYear(2019) returns 2 and dayOfYear(1,8,2019) returns 8?      firstDayOfYear(2019) + dayOfYear(1,8,2019)    This would return 10 but there are only 7 days of the week.      firstDayOfYear(2019) + dayOfYear(1,8,2019) - 1    This would return 9 but there are only 7 days of the week.      firstDayOfYear(2019) + dayOfYear(1,8,2019) % 7    Remember that % has precedence so this would return 2 + (8 % 7) = 2 + 1 = 3      firstDayOfYear(2019) + dayOfYear(1,8,2019) - 1 % 4    Remainder 4 does not make sense because there are 7 days of the week.      (firstDayOfYear(2019) + dayOfYear(1,8,2019) - 1) % 7    This would return (2 + 8 - 1) % 7 = 2.     "
