  "body": "  Which of the following correctly calls the method sentimentVal?      double value = sentimentVal();    sentimentVal takes a String argument and is in the class Review.      sentimentVal(\"terrible\");    sentimentVal returns a value and is in the class Review.      word.sentimentVal(\"terrible\");    sentimentVal returns a value and is a static method in the class Review.      double value = Review.sentimentVal(\"terrible\");    That's right1 sentimentVal takes a String argument and returns a double value and is a static method that can be called with the class name Review.      int value = sentimentVal(\"terrible\");    sentimentVal returns a double value, not int, and it's a static method in the class Review.     "
