  "number": "4.8.2",
  "title": "",
  "body": " An ArrayList is often called just a list. Prior to 2020 the AP CSA curriculum included interfaces which are somewhat like classes and the interface List was often used to declare a variable that would refer to an ArrayList . Interfaces are no longer on the exam, but if you see List being used in an old exam question just assume it’s an ArrayList .  "
