  "title": "",
  "body": "  How many times would the body of this nested for loop execute?  for (int row = 5; row <= 11; row++) for (int col = 3; col <= 18; col++)      11    Don't forget the inner loop.      11 - 5 = 6    Don't forget the inner loop.      (11 - 5) * (18 - 3) = 90    Notice that these loops use <=      (11 - 5 + 1) * (18 - 3 + 1) = 112    Yes, the loops do not start at 0 and use <=.     "
