  "type": "Note",
  "number": "5.6.2",
  "title": "",
  "body": " In Java an object variable has both a declared (compile-time) type and an actual (run-time) type . The declared (compile-time) type of a variable is the type that is used in the declaration. The actual (run-time) type is the class that actually creates the object using new.  "
