  "number": "5.11.2",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  Edit this code so the class Beagle is a subclass of the Dog class. When you run the code it should print “woof!” and then “arf arf”.    public class Dog { public void speak() { System.out.println(\"woof!\"); } public static void main(String[] args) { Dog d = new Dog(); d.speak(); Dog b = new Beagle(); b.speak(); } } class Beagle { public void speak() { System.out.println(\"arf arf\"); } }  import static org.junit.Assert.*; import org.junit.*; import java.io.*; public class RunestoneTests extends CodeTestHelper { @Test public void testMain() throws IOException { String output = getMethodOutput(\"main\"); String expect = \"woof!\\n\" + \"arf arf\\n\"; boolean passed = getResults(expect, output, \"Expected output from main\"); assertTrue(passed); } @Test public void testBeagleExtendsDog() { String target = \"class Beagle extends Dog\"; boolean passed = checkCodeContains(\"class Beagle extends class Dog\", target); assertTrue(passed); } }   "
