  "body": "  The fibonacci method is shown below. What is returned as a result of fibonacci(5) ?   public int fibonacci (int num) { if (num <= 1) return num; else return fibonacci(num - 1) + fibonacci(num - 2); }       5    fibonacci(5) returns fibonacci(4) + fibonacci(3). fibonacci(4) returns fibonacci(3) and fibonacci(2). fibonacci(3) returns fibonacci(2) + fibonacci(1). fibonacci(2) returns fibonacci(1) + fibonacci(0). fibonacci(1) returns 1, and fibonacci(0) returns 0. When the code is traced, 5 is returned.      6    Check your tracing to make sure that fibonacci(0) returned 0 and fibonacci(1) returned 1.      8    This is the answer returned for fibonacci(6). Check your tracing and try again.      13    This is the answer returned for fibonacci(7). Check your tracing and try again.      15    Notice what is returned in the if statement. fibonacci(0) returns 0, not 1.     "
