  "body": "  Which of the following is equivalent to ! (!(x >= 7) && (x > 2)) ?      (x >= 7) && (x > 2)    Use A and B to represent the expressions -- A becomes !(x >= 7), B becomes (x > 2). ! (A && B) does NOT equal !A && B.      (x < 7) && (x <= 2)    Use A and B to represent the expressions -- A becomes !(x >= 7), B becomes (x > 2). ! (A && B) does NOT equal A && !B. !(x >= 7) is the same as (x < 7).      (x >= 7) && (x < 2)    Use A and B to represent the expressions -- A becomes !(x >= 7), B becomes (x > 2). ! (A && B) does NOT equal !A && !B. Also, the negation of (x > 2) is (x <= 2), not (x < 2).      (x >= 7) || (x <= 2)    Use A and B to represent the expressions -- A becomes !(x >= 7), B becomes (x > 2). ! (A && B) is equal to !A || !B, according to DeMorgan's law. The negation of !(x >= 7) is (x >= 7), and the negation of (x > 2) is (x <= 2).      (x < 7) || (x < 2)    Use A and B to represent the expressions -- A becomes !(x >= 7), B becomes (x > 2). ! (A && B) does NOT equal A || !B. The negation of (x > 2) is (x <= 2), not (x < 2), and !(x >= 7) is the same as (x < 7).     "
