  "body": "  Write a method called countOccurrences that determines how many times a specific target string appears within a larger text string.  Be careful! It is easy to end up with an infinite loop if you are not careful when updating your loop variable. You will need to use the indexOf method to find the next occurrence of the target string, and then update your loop variable to start searching for the next occurrence after the current one.    public class PhraseAnalyzer { public static int countOccurrences(String text, String target) { } public static void main(String[] args) { \/\/ Test 1: Multiple occurrences String text1 = \"cat bat rat cat\"; String target1 = \"cat\"; System.out.println(\"Text: \" + text1 + \" | Target: \" + target1); System.out.println(\"Count: \" + PhraseAnalyzer.countOccurrences(text1, target1)); \/\/ Expected: 2 System.out.println(); \/\/ Test 2: Target not in text String text2 = \"The quick brown fox\"; String target2 = \"dog\"; System.out.println(\"Text: \" + text2 + \" | Target: \" + target2); System.out.println(\"Count: \" + PhraseAnalyzer.countOccurrences(text2, target2)); \/\/ Expected: 0 System.out.println(); \/\/ Test 3: Entire text is the target String text3 = \"Java\"; String target3 = \"Java\"; System.out.println(\"Text: \" + text3 + \" | Target: \" + target3); System.out.println(\"Count: \" + PhraseAnalyzer.countOccurrences(text3, target3)); \/\/ Expected: 1 } }  import static org.junit.Assert.*; import org.junit.*; import java.io.*; public class RunestoneTests extends CodeTestHelper { private String[] input1 = {\"aaaaa\", \"HELLO hello\", \"Red Blue Red\", \"Empty\", \"abc\"}; private String[] input2 = {\"aa\", \"hello\", \"Red\", \"a\", \"abcd\"}; private String[] expected = {\"2\", \"1\", \"2\", \"0\", \"0\"}; @Test public void test0() { boolean passed = test(0); assertTrue(passed); } @Test public void test1() { boolean passed = test(1); assertTrue(passed); } @Test public void test2() { boolean passed = test(2); assertTrue(passed); } @Test public void test3() { boolean passed = test(3); assertTrue(passed); } @Test public void test4() { boolean passed = test(4); assertTrue(passed); } private boolean test(int i) { String desc = \"countOccurrences(\\\"\" + input1[i] + \"\\\", \\\"\" + input2[i] + \"\\\")\"; String actual = \"\"; try { actual = \"\" + PhraseAnalyzer.countOccurrences(input1[i], input2[i]); } catch (Exception e) { actual = \"The code caused an exception\"; } boolean passed = getResults(expected[i],actual,desc); return passed; } private boolean stringMatch(String str1, String str2) { str1 = str1.replaceAll(\" \", \"\"); str2 = str2.replaceAll(\" \", \"\"); return str1.contains(str2); } }   "
