  "title": "",
  "body": "  The following program copies the first half of an array given as an argument to the method into a result array which is returned. But, the blocks have been mixed up and include one extra block that is not needed in a correct solution. Drag the blocks from the left and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check button to check your solution.     public static int[] firstHalf(int[] arr)  {    int[] result = new int[arr.length \/ 2];    for (int i = 0; i < result.length; i++)  {    for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++)  {    result[i] = arr[i];    } \/\/end for loop    return result;    } \/\/end firstHalf method    "
